🎨 Graph View Tips
 
- Color by tag → see clusters instantly
- Group by folder → separate projects
- Hide tags you don't need → reduce noise
- Click a node → highlight connections
 
 
 
⚠️ Common Mistakes to Avoid
 
❌ Mistake ✅ Fix 
Creating folders only → no links Folders organize files. Links organize ideas. Use both! 
Too many notes → no connections Spend 5 min/week adding links. Unlinked notes = invisible knowledge 
Duplicating the same topic in 5 notes One concept = One Note. Link to it instead of copying 
No MOCs → lost in notes Create 1 MOC per major area. Use it as your homepage 
Over-linking every word Link only when you want to reference that concept later 
No maintenance → messy vault Follow the weekly/monthly routine 
 
 
 
🚀 Quick Start Checklist
 
Create the folder structure above
Create your Home MOC →  MOC — Index.md 
Pick 3 most important topics → create 1 MOC for each
Link every existing note to at least one MOC
Set aside 5 min daily for linking new notes
Turn on Backlinks plugin in Obsidian
 
 
 
💡 Final Principle: A knowledge graph isn't built in a day — it grows one link at a time. Every connection you add today makes your future work faster. Start small, link consistently, watch your knowledge grow ✅
 
